+ * period equal to the path, an offset of zero): every arm reads 4 runs at 0.215 share in
+ * WebKit for a requested 0.05. Decimating the same pose walks it back — 492 segments → 4 runs,
+ * 123 → 1, and a perfectly straight 599-segment rectangle breaks identically, so it is not the
+ * wobble either. WebKit restarts the dash phase every ~128 segments of a polyline; Chromium
+ * dashes the path whole. A hand-drawn ring is ~490 segments by construction.
+ *
+ * So the front is not dashed. It is DRAWN: the pose is truncated at `fraction · length`, with
+ * the final point interpolated, and the renderer paints a path that ends exactly where the
