+/**
+ * Leading-edge rate gate on a front's commit: a write lands now when the window is clear (the
+ * front never lags the act by more than the window), and no two commits land closer than
+ * FRONT_MIN_MS on the clock's own grain — across runs too, so a restart, a snap or a rest pose
+ * is inside the budget like any frame. A `force`d write (a tween's exact end, a snap) is never
+ * dropped and never lands inside the window: it is owed, and lands at `last + FRONT_MIN_MS`, so
+ * a gauge and its a11y mirror still agree to the digit and the end costs no budget. A write
+ * that arrives while one is owed replaces its value (the latest is the truth).
