+/**
+ * A front's tween on the hand's clock (T9-M20 D10, the displacement clause): one pencil-boil
+ * `sequence` carries the rAF timeline and the tween's own clock advances by at most
+ * `MOTION.hand.stepMs` per tick, so a frame the main thread lost pauses the front for one
+ * frame's travel instead of landing it wherever the wall clock says. A healthy frame at any
+ * refresh rate ≥ 60 Hz is never slowed. `onComplete` fires when the tween's clock, not the
